# SHIPRAG System Architecture & Execution Workflow

This visual overview illustrates how the **SHIPRAG Backend Components** interact during document ingestion, token chunking, vector embedding, and hybrid search generation.

---

## 1. Complete End-to-End System Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph Client ["Client / Ingestion Layer"]
        CLI["CLI Tool / Web Dashboard"]
        GH["GitHub Push Webhooks"]
    end

    subgraph Auth ["Auth Service (:8001)"]
        JWT["JWT Auth & API Key Validation"]
        Tenant["Multi-Tenant Organization Isolation"]
    end

    subgraph Ingest ["Ingestion Service (:8002)"]
        Parser["Multi-Format Parser (.md, .pdf, .docx, .html)"]
        StreamProd["Redis Streams Producer ('doc-stream')"]
    end

    subgraph Worker ["Embedding Worker (:8003)"]
        StreamCons["Redis Streams Consumer"]
        Chunker["Token Chunker (app.core.chunking)"]
        Embedder["Embedding Model (text-embedding-3-small)"]
    end

    subgraph Storage ["Persistence Layer"]
        PGVector[("PostgreSQL + pgvector")]
        RedisCache[("Redis Cache")]
    end

    subgraph Search ["Retrieval Service (:8004)"]
        Hybrid["Hybrid Search (70% Vector + 30% Keyword BM25)"]
        LLM["LLM Generation (claude-sonnet-4-6)"]
        SSE["SSE Response Streaming"]
    end

    CLI -->|Request + Bearer Token| JWT
    GH -->|Webhook Event| Parser
    JWT --> Tenant --> Parser
    Parser -->|Raw Document| StreamProd
    StreamProd -->|Publish Event| StreamCons
    StreamCons --> Chunker
    Chunker -->|Tokens & Overlaps| Embedder
    Embedder -->|1536-dim Vectors| PGVector
    
    CLI -->|Query Request| Hybrid
    PGVector <-->|Dense Search| Hybrid
    RedisCache <-->|Cached Chunks| Hybrid
    Hybrid -->|Relevant Context| LLM
    LLM -->|Stream Answer| SSE
    SSE --> CLI
```

